 "_note": "THE SLOW JOURNEY -- 31 stations, authored as PLACES rather than a track (Ryan 2026-08-20: 'this could be a 20-minute 30-minute video just on this painting... a painting is not something you race through. It's about the journey.'). Each station names a place in MASTER px and two framings: WIDE (stand back and see the scene) and DETAIL (what the push goes in to look at). build-route.py turns these into camera keys using pacing laws -- never faster than the cap, zoom and dolly rate-limited -- so the FILM'S LENGTH EMERGES from the painting instead of being squeezed into a soundtrack. Every station was authored against a gridded crop of the master (evidence/band-*.png), so every detail target is a real thing in the painting. Silent: Ryan's narration is the soundtrack. GENERATED by build-route.py from stations-slow.json -- edit the stations, not this file.",
